#!/usr/bin/env xetal
## Arrays: dense arrays, 1-origin indexing, the structural built-ins and
## scalar extension. Run it with "xetal run demos/arrays.xtl" (or
## "./demos/arrays.xtl"); it prints the result of each line after the
## definition of m: the matrix, its shape, a row, the last row, the
## matrix times ten, a row joined to more items and powers of ten.
## Read it for how r_eshape, s_elect, t_ake and c_at treat a matrix.

### The matrix

## m: a 2 by 3 matrix holding 1 to 6, row by row.
m := 2 3 r_eshape r_ange 6

### Structural built-ins and scalar extension

m
s_hape m
2 s_elect m
-1 t_ake m
m * 10
(f_irst m) c_at 7 8 9
10 ^ o_ffsets 3
